  "terminal": {
    "change": "Prepare a nonnegative packed rank after full quantity validation; compare it once per stable merge decision. Reuse the sorted buffer for retained routes and the other merge buffer for the query envelope.",
    "removed_array_allocations": 2,
    "proof": {
      "packing": "Each raw coordinate is <512; the two9-bit fields and output field are disjoint. The nonnegative26-bit packed number has exactly the lexicographic order of(-output,raw1,raw2). Equal keys retain left-run priority.",
      "comparisons": "In each bottom-up merge the right run has length<=left. At least right_length comparisons are needed. Summing right-run membership over widths counts set bits of indices0..N-1: Cmin(N)=sum popcount(i). Descending comparator order attains it.",
      "range": "ForN=16+r,1<=r<=16:2Cmin-3N=16-r+2Cmin(r)>=0. ForN=32+r,1<=r<=32:2Cmin-3N=64-r+2Cmin(r)>0. Explicit48-size enumeration has minimum saving15.",
      "alias": "Keep both original/scratch references; pick envelope by reference identity of returned ordered. Capture ordered[read] before retained write; retainedCount<=read, so no future ordered element is overwritten. Envelope is a distinct array and only its initialized prefix is read. Search uses retained count, not array length.",
      "budget": "With identical admitted routes/comparator outcomes/Pareto decisions/search sequence, full successful-path work delta is5N-2N-2C=3N-2C<=-15. Therefore an additive remaining-work budget sufficient for the old full success is sufficient for the new full success, although individual charge values, positions, early refusals and checkpoints differ.",
      "limits": "This proves structural ordering/alias and additive work sufficiency, not CPU speed, identical wall-clock cancellation, arbitrary callback-injection equivalence, or a universal allocator bound."
    },
